  "river_and_transport": {
    "_doc": "EVERY RECONSTRUCTED HEAD AT A RIVER OR TRANSPORT TRADE, and the house of trade behind it or the reason there is none. `kind` says which sort of absence a headless trade is: `house_of_trade` this programme builds, `count_already_held` the register already over-holds, `employment` has no premises to keep, `deferred` waits on the ticket named. No head is passed over in silence — that is what this table is for.",
    "ticket": "T-1424",
    "trades": 9,
    "heads": 20,
    "heads_this_programme_owes_a_house": 0,
    "rows": [
      {
        "trade": "boatman",
        "kind": "employment",
        "deferred_to": null,
        "heads": 3,
        "why": "NO PREMISES. A boatman is a hand on the water — the ferry at the forks, the lighters working the bar, the river craft. T-1189 seats him.",
        "people": [
          {
            "person_id": "rc_dufresne_hyacinthe",
            "name": "Hyacinthe Dufresne",
            "division": "north",
            "head_slot": "trade_households:persons/male/20_29/north/family/trade:boatman:004",
            "firm": null
          },
          {
            "person_id": "rc_bourassa_hyacinthe",
            "name": "Hyacinthe Bourassa",
            "division": "south",
            "head_slot": "trade_households:persons/male/20_29/south/family/trade:boatman:008",
            "firm": null
          },
          {
            "person_id": "rc_robillard_michel",
            "name": "Michel Robillard",
            "division": "south",
            "head_slot": "trade_households:persons/male/30_39/south/family/trade:boatman:005",
            "firm": null
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "trade": "forwarding_and_commission",
        "kind": "count_already_held",
        "deferred_to": null,
        "heads": 2,
        "why": "NO ESTABLISHMENT TO ORDER, AND THAT IS NOT THE SAME AS NO MAN TO PLACE. The December 1835 State census prints four storage and forwarding houses and the register holds EIGHT at the scene date, so `businesses/storage_and_forwarding` leaves nothing to reconstruct and the 'gap beyond the attested four' T-1409 went looking for is not there. The resident band still drew these heads, and rightly: it draws against the PERSON buckets, off the 1839 trade table's share of men at a trade, and a town can be short of forwarding clerks while holding twice the houses it was counted for. So these men are hands at houses that already stand, and T-1189 seats them; a firm minted here would be a ninth house against a count of four.",
        "people": [
          {
            "person_id": "rc_fisk_abner",
            "name": "Abner Fisk",
            "division": "south",
            "head_slot": "trade_households:persons/male/20_29/south/family/trade:forwarding_and_commission:033",
            "firm": null
          },
          {
            "person_id": "rc_bertrand_louis",
            "name": "Louis Bertrand",
            "division": "west",
            "head_slot": "trade_households:persons/male/20_29/west/family/trade:forwarding_and_commission:013",
            "firm": null
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "trade": "livery_stable_keeper",
        "kind": "house_of_trade",
        "deferred_to": null,
        "heads": 2,
        "why": "the trade names the house; this programme builds one per head.",
